Addresses code review feedback to extract hardcoded vertical boundary values (-20, +20) for weather particle respawn logic into a named constant.

**Changes:**
- Added `particleVerticalRange` configuration property (value: 20) to define vertical boundaries of weather effects relative to player position
- Replaced magic number literals in particle boundary check with reference to the constant

```javascript
// Before
if (positions[i * 3 + 1] < playerPos.y - 20) {
    positions[i * 3 + 1] = playerPos.y + 20;

// After  
if (positions[i * 3 + 1] < playerPos.y - this.particleVerticalRange) {
    positions[i * 3 + 1] = playerPos.y + this.particleVerticalRange;
```

Improves maintainability by centralizing the vertical range configuration alongside other system parameters like `particleCount` and `range`.

